---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DownloadPanel from '../components/DownloadPanel.astro';
import RelatedLinks from '../components/RelatedLinks.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Download AliasMode Free"
  description="Download the free, open-source AliasMode Windows beta. Create unlimited browser profiles and sign up inside the app for Cloud sync and team collaboration."
>
  <section class="download-hero">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Free Windows beta</p>
      <h1>Download AliasMode. Start free.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Install AliasMode, choose Cloud, and create your free account inside the app. You can then synchronize profiles across devices and invite your team.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="onboarding">
      <li><span>1</span><div><strong>Download</strong><small>Get the Windows beta.</small></div></li>
      <li><span>2</span><div><strong>Launch</strong><small>Open AliasMode.</small></div></li>
      <li><span>3</span><div><strong>Sign up</strong><small>Choose Cloud in the app.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <DownloadPanel />

  <section class="after-install">
    <h2>After installation</h2>
    <div class="grid"><article class="card"><strong>Install CloakBrowser</strong><p>AliasMode installs the separately licensed browser runtime used to open profiles.</p></article><article class="card"><strong>Create unlimited profiles</strong><p>Give each account, client, brand, or project its own browser profile.</p></article><article class="card"><strong>Turn on Cloud sync</strong><p>Create your free account inside AliasMode to synchronize portable profiles.</p></article><article class="card"><strong>Invite your team</strong><p>Use one workspace with owner and member roles for collaboration.</p></article></div>
  </section>

  <section class="install-notes">
    <p class="eyebrow">Windows installation</p>
    <h2>Check your download before you run it.</h2>
    <p>The Windows beta is unsigned, so SmartScreen can warn about unsigned or uncommon software.</p>
    <ol><li>Open the GitHub release URL and check that it is under <code>github.com/aliasmode/aliasmode</code>.</li><li>Verify the downloaded file against the published SHA-256 checksum.</li><li>If Windows shows SmartScreen, select <strong>More info</strong>, then <strong>Run anyway</strong> only if you accept the risk and Windows offers that option.</li></ol>
    <p>Do not disable Windows protection. A checksum helps verify a downloaded file. It does not sign the app.</p>
  </section>

  <RelatedLinks paths={['/docs/getting-started/', '/docs/cloakbrowser/', '/security/']} title="Install and verify AliasMode" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .download-hero { align-items: end; display: grid; gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem); grid-template-columns: 1fr .8fr; margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .download-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 5.6vw, 4.6rem); }
  .onboarding { list-style: none; margin: 0; max-width: none; padding: 0; }
  .onboarding li { align-items: center; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); display: grid; gap: 1rem; grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr; margin: 0; padding: .9rem 0; }
  .onboarding li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .onboarding li > span { color: var(--violet); font: 700 .72rem/1 var(--font-mono); }
  .onboarding div { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .onboarding small { color: var(--ink-3); }
  .after-install { margin: 5rem 0; }
  .after-install > h2, .install-notes h2 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.6vw, 3rem); }
  .after-install .card strong { color: var(--violet-ink); }
  .after-install .card p { color: var(--ink-2); font-size: .9rem; }
  .install-notes { background: var(--violet-soft); border-left: .35rem solid var(--violet); border-radius: 0 var(--r-lg) var(--r-lg) 0; padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  @media (max-width: 48rem) { .download-hero { gap: 2rem; grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
